(1) Directly after the block `:root[data-color-mode="dark"] { ... }` (it ends at about line 169, before the comment 'A logo for each set of colours') add, unlayered like the blocks above it:

/*
 * The admin's colour roles outside the admin (bloat review step 0.34, docs/admin-style.md section 4). A few admin parts are drawn on
 * public pages (ActionForm and its buttons on /status, /report, sign-up and get-domain; the print button on a hosted invoice; the
 * on-site editor's toolbar, text styles, colour field and modal). There the roles follow the site's own colours, as admin.css gives the
 * site's names the roles' values inside the admin. The selector never matches inside the admin, so the two can never form a loop.
 * Shop and site code still writes the site's names: src/lib/stylesheet-sources.scan.test.ts holds both rules.
 */
html:not([data-admin]) {
  --canvas: var(--background);
  --card: var(--background);
  --sunken: var(--surface);
  --line: var(--border);
  --edge: var(--border);
  --ink: var(--foreground);
  --ink-2: var(--muted);
  --inverse: var(--foreground);
  --inverse-ink: var(--background);
  --brand: var(--accent);
  --brand-ink: var(--accent-foreground);
  --danger-text: #b91c1c;
  --warning-text: #b45309;
}
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  html:not([data-admin]):not([data-color-mode="light"]) {
    --danger-text: #f87171;
    --warning-text: #fbbf24;
  }
}
html:not([data-admin])[data-color-mode="dark"] {
  --danger-text: #f87171;
  --warning-text: #fbbf24;
}

(2) Rewrite the comment inside the @theme block above `--color-canvas: var(--canvas);` (it says 'Outside the admin nothing sets them, so they are for admin pages only.') to: 'The admin's colour roles (docs/admin-style.md section 4), set inside the admin by its scheme (`src/app/admin/schemes/*.css`). Outside the admin the thirteen that shared admin parts read follow the site's own colours (the html:not([data-admin]) block below); shop and site code writes the site's names, never these.' Do not change any `--color-*` line.
